## Why This Question Is Asked
This evaluates your ability to validate a production-grade streaming ML pipeline under realistic conditions, covering data integrity, performance under load, drift handling, and safe deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end streaming test strategies and synthetic data generation
- Backpressure handling and consumer lag in Kafka/Flink
- Feature drift detection and model retraining triggers
- Canary rollouts, shadow traffic, and safe rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// End-to-end test harness wiring synthetic replay, latency tracking,
// and assertion validation
async function runE2ETest(config) {
  const syntheticData = generateLabeledAnomalies(config);
  const results = await pipeline.process(syntheticData);

  const latency = measureLatency(results);
  assert(latency.p95 < 300, 'P95 latency exceeded budget');
  assert(latency.p99 < 1000, 'P99 latency exceeded budget');

  const correctness = validateChecksums(results);
  assert(correctness, 'Data correctness check failed');

  return { latency, correctness };
}
```

## Interview Context
This question assesses practical TDD implementation skills for API testing, requiring knowledge of testing frameworks, mocking strategies, and development workflow.

## Key Concepts
- **Red-Green-Refactor Cycle**: Write failing tests, implement minimal passing code, refactor while maintaining test coverage
- **Jest Testing Framework**: Structure tests with describe/it blocks, setup/teardown hooks, assertions
- **Supertest Integration**: HTTP assertions for Express endpoints, request/response testing
- **Mock Implementation**: Isolate external dependencies using jest.mock() and manual mocks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Red phase - failing test
describe('POST /api/users', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    jest.mock('../services/emailService')
  })

  it('should create user and return 201', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .post('/api/users')
      .send({ email: 'test@example.com', name: 'John' })
      .expect(201)

    expect(response.body).toHaveProperty('id')
    expect(response.body.email).toBe('test@example.com')
  })
})

// Green phase - minimal implementation
app.post('/api/users', async (req, res) => {
  const user = await User.create(req.body)
  res.status(201).json(user)
})

// Refactor phase - extract validation, add error handling
```

